action — rollback drops all three effects, commit lands then pokes\\\",\\\"work-queue.test.ts: re-enqueue at later source version resets form row to pending at that version\\\",\\\"thread-migration.test.ts: FC-0.5 v5 over a populated Epic 01 file — records intact, columns defaulted, F-02 backfill present, post-migration intake works\\\"],\\\"modified\\\":[\\\"work-queue.test.ts: 17 work-item id literals gained -v1 (sanctioned Story 0 amendment)\\\",\\\"cli-process-work-queue.test.ts: 2 work-item id literals gained -v1 (sanctioned Story 0 amendment)\\\",\\\"thread-migration.test.ts: 2 schemaVersionOf assertions 4→5 (mechanical consequence of migration v5 landing)\\\"],\\\"removed\\\":[],\\\"totalAfterStory\\\":155,\\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\":23},\\\"gatesRun\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm run green-verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm run verify-all\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"}],\\\"selfReview\\\":{\\\"passesRun\\\":0,\\\"findingsFixed\\\":[\\\"Tech design's idx_work_item_queue named rowid as an index column; SQLite rejects rowid in index definitions — index now covers (status, eligible_at), claimNext keeps ORDER BY rowid at query time\\\",\\\"damagedSourceThread originally corrupted a fully-closed thread, yielding one open turn (not corrupt); builder now leaves a turn open through real intake before the corruption write so two open turns exist\\\",\\\"Initial Lhc construction stubbed the threads/intakeStream namespaces incorrectly; fixed to wire the real domain namespaces\\\"],\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\":[\\\"The scheduler poke seam (setSchedulerPoke/fireSchedulerPoke) lives in shared/context.ts rather than scheduler.ts: scheduler.ts will import domain handler tables from Story 1, and a work-queue→scheduler import would then cycle through domains→tech-utils. Story 1 should install the real scheduler into this seam at createSdk\\\",\\\"createSdk does not yet install its scheduler into the poke seam (manual mode's poke is a no-op by contract and background drain doesn't exist); background-mode wiring is explicitly Story 1's per the story boundary\\\",\\\"enqueue takes caller-supplied form targets to keep the queue util domain-blind; the kind→form mapping lives in the owning domains (MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS includes tool_call_summary ready for Story 2, though intake's kind gate still excludes tool_call as required)\\\",\\\"multi-state/damaged-source fixtures use the sanctioned below-SDK setFormState writer (UPDATE-only, mirroring the production completion contract) since ready/failed/blocked are unreachable until Stories 1–3 — the known cross-story golden-shaped debt from coverage.md\\\",\\\"WorkHandler's item parameter is typed structurally in shared/derivation.ts (not as the util's WorkItemRecord) to keep shared→tech-utils dependency one-directional; Story 1 may want to tighten this when the drain dispatches for real\\\"]},\\\"openQuestions\\\":[\\\"thread-migration.test.ts's two schemaVersionOf(...).toBe(4) assertions necessarily became toBe(5) when migration v5 landed. The test plan's sanctioned-amendment list names only the work-item id literals, and says further Epic 01 edits are a ruling, not an edit. I treated the version-number bump as a mechanical consequence of the story's own deliverable (the file is also a named Story 0 implementation target) and made the edit; please ratify or rule.\\\"],\\\"specDeviations\\\":[\\\"idx_work_item_queue created as (status, eligible_at) instead of the tech design's (status, eligible_at, rowid): SQLite forbids rowid inside an index definition; head selection still orders by rowid at query time\\\",\\\"Sanctioned id amendment executed: 17 'w-…' literals in test/work-queue.test.ts and 2 in test/cli-process-work-queue.test.ts gained the -v1 suffix; red manifest regenerated for both files plus thread-migration.test.ts and fixtures.test.ts\\\",\\\"thread-migration.test.ts schema-version assertions updated 4→5 (see openQuestions)\\\",\\\"Scheduler poke seam placed in shared/context.ts rather than inside scheduler.ts to avoid a future import cycle (work-queue→scheduler→domains→tech-utils); DD-5 semantics (poke registered on ctx.onCommit by enqueue, transactional by construction) are unchanged\\\",\\\"CLI provider resolution (DD-11) not landed in this story: no CLI command needs a provider until drain (Story 1); the named-provider registry ships with it\\\"],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"Verify Story 0, ratify the schema-version assertion amendment, then proceed to Story 1 (queue execution): claimNext/complete/failAttempt SQL, drain, lease/reclaim, background scheduling installing the real scheduler into the shared poke seam, and the DD-11 CLI provider registry.\\\"},\\\"errors\\\":[],\\\"warnings\\\":[],\\\"artifacts\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"result-envelope\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/003-implementor.json\\\"}],\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T03:01:39.040Z\\\",\\\"finishedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T03:23:15.126Z\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:44:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\texport type ErrorClass = \\\"caller_error\\\" | \\\"state_corruption\\\" | \\\"system_error\\\";\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\texport type ErrorCode =\\n     4\\t  | \\\"path_exists\\\"\\n     5\\t  | \\\"thread_not_found\\\"\\n     6\\t  | \\\"invalid_thread_ref\\\" // empty/blank file path or otherwise unusable reference\\n     7\\t  | \\\"invalid_event\\\"\\n     8\\t  | \\\"empty_batch\\\"\\n     9\\t  | \\\"empty_stdin\\\" // CLI adapter only, emitted before any SDK call\\n    10\\t  | \\\"turn_state_corrupt\\\"\\n    11\\t  | \\\"storage_failure\\\"\\n    12\\t  // Epic 02 (tech design §Interfaces, issue 4):\\n    13\\t  | \\\"turn_open\\\" // caller_error — mutation against an open turn\\n    14\\t  | \\\"message_initiates_turn\\\" // caller_error — delete refused toward turns.delete\\n    15\\t  | \\\"message_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n    16\\t  | \\\"turn_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n    17\\t  | \\\"unknown_work_kind\\\" // state_corruption — unregistered kind at dispatch\\n    18\\t  | \\\"provider_failure\\\" // system_error — exhausted retries; form.reason carries detail\\n    19\\t  | \\\"source_damaged\\\"; // state_corruption — handler found corrupt source; form blocked\\n    20\\t\\n    21\\texport interface ErrorResult {\\n    22\\t  errorClass: ErrorClass;\\n    23\\t  code: ErrorCode;\\n    24\\t  reason: string; // human-readable; machine logic switches on code\\n    25\\t  eventIndex?: number; // present on batch validation failures\\n    26\\t}\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t// Expected operational failures — caller errors, corruption, environment\\n    29\\t// failures — are always returned as OpResult errors, never thrown.\\n    30\\t// Programmer bugs inside lhc may still throw; callers are not expected\\n    31\\t// to handle throws as contract outcomes.\\n    32\\texport type OpResult<T> =\\n    33\\t  | { ok: true; value: T }\\n    34\\t  | { ok: false; error: ErrorResult };\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t// Infrastructure failures (SQLite, fs) are expected operational outcomes,\\n    37\\t// caught at the operation boundary and wrapped with the underlying detail.\\n    38\\texport function storageFailure(reason: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n    39\\t  return {\\n    40\\t    ok: false,\\n    41\\t    error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason },\\n    42\\t  };\\n    43\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:46:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\timport { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\texport interface Migration {\\n     4\\t  version: number; // 1-based, strictly increasing\\n     5\\t  statements: readonly string[];\\n     6\\t}\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\texport function openDatabase(path: string): DatabaseSync {\\n     9\\t  const db = new DatabaseSync(path);\\n    10\\t  db.exec(\\\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;\\\");\\n    11\\t  db.exec(\\\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\\\");\\n    12\\t  db.exec(\\\"PRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000;\\\");\\n    13\\t  db.exec(\\\"PRAGMA synchronous = NORMAL;\\\");\\n    14\\t  return db;\\n    15\\t}\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t// Epic 02's single migration (tech design §Storage): queue mechanical fields\\n    18\\t// on the existing work_item table, the derived_form state table, the chunk\\n    19\\t// tables, and the projection-level delete stamps. The whole epic's schema\\n    20\\t// lands in one version — behavior arrives story by story. Assembled into the\\n    21\\t// thread-file migration history by threads/internal/create.ts.\\n    22\\texport const MIGRATION_V5_STATEMENTS: readonly string[] = [\\n    23\\t  // claim mechanics on the existing table (DD-1: no disposition column —\\n    24\\t  // queue rows are live work only; terminal rows are deleted and their\\n    25\\t  // outcomes reported in-memory; durable outcome state lives on derived_form)\\n    26\\t  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;`,\\n    27\\t  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN last_error TEXT;`,\\n    28\\t  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN claimed_at TEXT;`,\\n    29\\t  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN claim_expires_at TEXT;`,\\n    30\\t  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN eligible_at TEXT;`, // backoff gate; NULL = immediately eligible\\n    31\\t  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN payload TEXT;`, // JSON: { sourceVersion?, form? }; id format includes sourceVersion\\n    32\\t  // Tech design sketches (status, eligible_at, rowid); SQLite forbids rowid\\n    33\\t  // inside an index definition, so the index covers the two real columns and\\n    34\\t  // claimNext's ORDER BY rowid walks the head as before.\\n    35\\t  `CREATE INDEX idx_work_item_queue ON work_item (status, eligible_at);`,\\n    36\\t  `CREATE TABLE derived_form (\\n    37\\t    subject_kind TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (subject_kind IN ('message','turn','chunk')),\\n    38\\t    subject_id   TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    39\\t    form         TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    40\\t    state        TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (state IN ('pending','ready','failed','blocked')),\\n    41\\t    content      TEXT,\\n    42\\t    reason       TEXT,\\n    43\\t    metadata     TEXT,\\n    44\\t    source_version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\\n    45\\t    gaps         TEXT,\\n    46\\t    derived_at   TEXT,\\n    47\\t    PRIMARY KEY (subject_kind, subject_id, form)\\n    48\\t  );`,\\n    49\\t  `CREATE TABLE chunk (\\n    50\\t    chunk_id     TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n    51\\t    chunk_order  INTEGER NOT NULL UNIQUE,\\n    52\\t    status       TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('open','closed')),\\n    53\\t    accumulated_projected_tokens INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\\n    54\\t  );`,\\n    55\\t  `CREATE TABLE chunk_member (\\n    56\\t    chunk_id   TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES chunk(chunk_id),\\n    57\\t    turn_id    TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE REFERENCES turns(turn_id),\\n    58\\t    member_idx INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n    59\\t    PRIMARY KEY (chunk_id, member_idx)\\n    60\\t  );`,\\n    61\\t  // projection-level delete (the record keeps everything; reads filter)\\n    62\\t  `ALTER TABLE message ADD COLUMN deleted_at TEXT;`,\\n    63\\t  `ALTER TABLE turns   ADD COLUMN deleted_at TEXT;`,\\n    64\\t  // F-02 backfill: pending form rows for work queued before v5 existed, so\\n    65\\t  // UPDATE-only completion finds them (row missing must mean deleted).\\n    66\\t  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n    67\\t    SELECT 'message', json_extract(source_ref, '$.messageId'), 'smoothed_prompt', 'pending', 1\\n    68\\t    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'prompt_smoothing';`,\\n    69\\t  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n    70\\t    SELECT 'message', json_extract(source_ref, '$.messageId'), 'tool_result_summary', 'pending', 1\\n    71\\t    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'tool_result_summary';`,\\n    72\\t  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n    73\\t    SELECT 'turn', json_extract(source_ref, '$.turnId'), 'turn_rendering', 'pending', 1\\n    74\\t    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'turn_derivation';`,\\n    75\\t  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n    76\\t    SELECT 'turn', json_extract(source_ref, '$.turnId'), 'lower_band_projection', 'pending', 1\\n    77\\t    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'turn_derivation';`,\\n    78\\t];\\n    79\\t\\n    80\\texport function getSchemaVersion(db: DatabaseSync): number {\\n    81\\t  const row = db.prepare(\\\"PRAGMA user_version\\\").get() as\\n    82\\t    | { user_version: number | bigint }\\n    83\\t    | undefined;\\n    84\\t  return Number(row?.user_version ?? 0);\\n    85\\t}\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\texport function runMigrations(\\n    88\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n    89\\t  migrations: readonly Migration[],\\n    90\\t): void {\\n    91\\t  let current = getSchemaVersion(db);\\n    92\\t  const ordered = [...migrations].sort((a, b) => a.version - b.version);\\n    93\\t  for (const migration of ordered) {\\n    94\\t    if (migration.version <= current) continue;\\n    95\\t    db.exec(\\\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\\\");\\n    96\\t    try {\\n    97\\t      for (const statement of migration.statements) db.exec(statement);\\n    98\\t      db.exec(`PRAGMA user_version = ${migration.version};`);\\n    99\\t      db.exec(\\\"COMMIT;\\\");\\n   100\\t    } catch (cause) {\\n   101\\t      db.exec(\\\"ROLLBACK;\\\");\\n   102\\t      throw cause;\\n   103\\t    }\\n   104\\t    current = migration.version;\\n   105\\t  }\\n   106\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:60:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_28\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\timport { randomBytes } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\n     2\\timport { rmSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n     3\\timport { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n     4\\timport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\n     5\\timport {\\n     6\\t  getSchemaVersion,\\n     7\\t  MIGRATION_V5_STATEMENTS,\\n     8\\t  openDatabase,\\n     9\\t  runMigrations,\\n    10\\t  type Migration,\\n    11\\t} from \\\"../../../shared/storage.js\\\";\\n    12\\timport { TOKEN_ESTIMATOR_ID } from \\\"../../../tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t// The one random id: its uniqueness scope is global across files and\\n    15\\t// registries (design decision 7).\\n    16\\texport function generateThreadId(): string {\\n    17\\t  return `th_${randomBytes(8).toString(\\\"hex\\\")}`;\\n    18\\t}\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t// The thread-file schema as a versioned history, never rewritten in place:\\n    21\\t// v1 is the Story 2 schema exactly as accepted (thread_metadata + event), and\\n    22\\t// each later story appends a version. Existing files upgrade lazily through\\n    23\\t// openThreadDatabase, so a file recorded under an earlier story is always\\n    24\\t// usable by a later one (F-03-001).\\n    25\\t//\\n    26\\t// Creation-time metadata values are interpolated through buildThreadMigrations\\n    27\\t// for new files only; existing files already hold their metadata row and the\\n    28\\t// upgrade path never touches it.\\n    29\\tfunction buildThreadMigrations(\\n    30\\t  metadata?: { threadId: string; createdAt: string },\\n    31\\t): Migration[] {\\n    32\\t  const metadataInsert =\\n    33\\t    metadata === undefined\\n    34\\t      ? []\\n    35\\t      : [\\n    36\\t          // Interpolated values are all generated by us (hex id, ISO\\n    37\\t          // timestamp, estimator constant) — never caller input.\\n    38\\t          `INSERT INTO thread_metadata (id, thread_id, created_at, token_estimator)\\n    39\\t           VALUES (1, '${metadata.threadId}', '${metadata.createdAt}', '${TOKEN_ESTIMATOR_ID}');`,\\n    40\\t        ];\\n    41\\t  return [\\n    42\\t    {\\n    43\\t      version: 1,\\n    44\\t      statements: [\\n    45\\t        `CREATE TABLE thread_metadata (\\n    46\\t          id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY CHECK (id = 1),\\n    47\\t          thread_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    48\\t          created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    49\\t          token_estimator TEXT NOT NULL\\n    50\\t        );`,\\n    51\\t        ...metadataInsert,\\n    52\\t        `CREATE TABLE event (\\n    53\\t          event_order INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n    54\\t          event_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    55\\t          idempotency_key TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\\n    56\\t          actor TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    57\\t          harness TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    58\\t          payload TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    59\\t          recorded_at TEXT NOT NULL\\n    60\\t        );`,\\n    61\\t      ],\\n    62\\t    },\\n    63\\t    {\\n    64\\t      version: 2, // Story 3: message projection\\n    65\\t      statements: [\\n    66\\t        `CREATE TABLE message (\\n    67\\t          message_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n    68\\t          source_event_order INTEGER NOT NULL UNIQUE REFERENCES event(event_order),\\n    69\\t          kind TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    70\\t          token_estimate INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n    71\\t          actor TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    72\\t          harness TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    73\\t          turn_id TEXT\\n    74\\t        );`,\\n    75\\t        `CREATE TABLE message_block (\\n    76\\t          message_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES message(message_id),\\n    77\\t          block_index INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n    78\\t          block_type TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    79\\t          content TEXT NOT NULL,\\n    80\\t          PRIMARY KEY (message_id, block_index)\\n    81\\t        );`,\\n    82\\t      ],\\n    83\\t    },\\n    84\\t    {\\n    85\\t      version: 3, // Story 4: turn state machine\\n    86\\t      statements: [\\n    87\\t        `CREATE TABLE turns (\\n    88\\t          turn_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n    89\\t          turn_order INTEGER NOT NULL UNIQUE,\\n    90\\t          status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('open', 'closed')),\\n    91\\t          opened_at_event_order INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n    92\\t          closed_at_event_order INTEGER\\n    93\\t        );`,\\n    94\\t      ],\\n    95\\t    },\\n    96\\t    {\\n    97\\t      version: 4, // Story 5: derivation work queueing\\n    98\\t      statements: [\\n    99\\t        // Work items live in the thread file and commit with the batch —\\n   100\\t        // not a separate database, not a separate transaction. status is\\n   101\\t        // unconstrained TEXT: this epic only ever writes 'queued'; the\\n   102\\t        // claim/lease statuses are Epic 02's to add.\\n   103\\t        `CREATE TABLE work_item (\\n   104\\t          work_item_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n   105\\t          owner TEXT NOT NULL,\\n   106\\t          kind TEXT NOT NULL,\\n   107\\t          source_ref TEXT NOT NULL,\\n   108\\t          status TEXT NOT NULL,\\n   109\\t          queued_at TEXT NOT NULL\\n   110\\t        );`,\\n   111\\t      ],\\n   112\\t    },\\n   113\\t    {\\n   114\\t      version: 5, // Epic 02 Story 0: queue mechanical fields, derived_form,\\n   115\\t      // chunk tables, deleted_at stamps, F-02 pending-row backfill — the\\n   116\\t      // epic's single migration (tech design §Storage), statements owned by\\n   117\\t      // shared/storage.ts.\\n   118\\t      statements: MIGRATION_V5_STATEMENTS,\\n   119\\t    },\\n   120\\t  ];\\n   121\\t}\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\tfunction notAThreadFile(filePath: string, detail: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n   124\\t  return {\\n   125\\t    ok: false,\\n   126\\t    error: {\\n   127\\t      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   128\\t      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n   129\\t      reason: `file at ${filePath} exists but is not an lhc thread file (${detail})`,\\n   130\\t    },\\n   131\\t  };\\n   132\\t}\\n   133\\t\\n   134\\tfunction errorDetail(cause: unknown): string {\\n   135\\t  return cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   136\\t}\\n   137\\t\\n   138\\t// Identity check before any migration runs, on a read-only handle so an\\n   139\\t// invalid file cannot be mutated by the probe itself (F-03-002): a thread\\n   140\\t// file always carries schema version >= 1 and the thread_metadata singleton\\n   141\\t// row that creation wrote transactionally. Anything else — an empty\\n   142\\t// database, an unrelated SQLite file, a non-database file — is rejected as a\\n   143\\t// caller error, never adopted.\\n   144\\tfunction validateThreadFile(filePath: string): { ok: true } | { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n   145\\t  let db: DatabaseSync | undefined;\\n   146\\t  try {\\n   147\\t    db = new DatabaseSync(filePath, { readOnly: true });\\n   148\\t    if (getSchemaVersion(db) < 1) {\\n   149\\t      return notAThreadFile(filePath, \\\"no lhc schema version\\\");\\n   150\\t    }\\n   151\\t    const table = db\\n   152\\t      .prepare(\\\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = 'table' AND name = 'thread_metadata'\\\")\\n   153\\t      .get();\\n   154\\t    if (table === undefined) {\\n   155\\t      return notAThreadFile(filePath, \\\"no thread_metadata table\\\");\\n   156\\t    }\\n   157\\t    const row = db.prepare(\\\"SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1\\\").get();\\n   158\\t    if (row === undefined) {\\n   159\\t      return notAThreadFile(filePath, \\\"no thread metadata row\\\");\\n   160\\t    }\\n   161\\t    return { ok: true };\\n   162\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   163\\t    const detail = errorDetail(cause);\\n   164\\t    // SQLite refusing the file as a database is an identity failure, not an\\n   165\\t    // environment failure; everything else stays a system error.\\n   166\\t    if (detail.includes(\\\"not a database\\\")) {\\n   167\\t      return notAThreadFile(filePath, detail);\\n   168\\t    }\\n   169\\t    return storageFailure(`could not inspect thread file: ${detail}`);\\n   170\\t  } finally {\\n   171\\t    db?.close();\\n   172\\t  }\\n   173\\t}\\n   174\\t\\n   175\\t// Opens a thread file and brings its schema to the current version before\\n   176\\t// returning the handle. Every SDK operation on an existing thread file goes\\n   177\\t// through here, so a pre-Story-3 file gains the message tables on its first\\n   178\\t// open by newer code — but only after the file proves it is a thread file;\\n   179\\t// migration never creates lhc schema on an arbitrary existing file. Each\\n   180\\t// migration runs in its own transaction (storage helper), completing before\\n   181\\t// any caller transaction begins.\\n   182\\texport function openThreadDatabase(filePath: string): OpResult<DatabaseSync> {\\n   183\\t  const valid = validateThreadFile(filePath);\\n   184\\t  if (!valid.ok) return valid;\\n   185\\t  let db: DatabaseSync;\\n   186\\t  try {\\n   187\\t    db = openDatabase(filePath);\\n   188\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   189\\t    return storageFailure(`could not open thread file: ${errorDetail(cause)}`);\\n   190\\t  }\\n   191\\t  try {\\n   192\\t    runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations());\\n   193\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   194\\t    db.close();\\n   195\\t    return storageFailure(`thread schema migration failed: ${errorDetail(cause)}`);\\n   196\\t  }\\n   197\\t  return { ok: true, value: db };\\n   198\\t}\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\t// Schema v1 plus the metadata row land in one migration transaction, so the\\n   201\\t// file either has its full schema and metadata row or creation fails whole.\\n   202\\texport function createThreadFile(\\n   203\\t  filePath: string,\\n   204\\t  threadId: string,\\n   205\\t  createdAt: string,\\n   206\\t): void {\\n   207\\t  const db = openDatabase(filePath);\\n   208\\t  try {\\n   209\\t    runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations({ threadId, createdAt }));\\n   210\\t  } finally {\\n   211\\t    db.close();\\n   212\\t  }\\n   213\\t}\\n   214\\t\\n   215\\t// Compensation: removes the thread file and its WAL companions. Used when the\\n   216\\t// registry insert fails after file creation (no registry row without its\\n   217\\t// file) and when file creation itself fails partway.\\n   218\\texport function deleteThreadFile(filePath: string): void {\\n   219\\t  for (const suffix of [\\\"\\\", \\\"-wal\\\", \\\"-shm\\\"]) {\\n   220\\t    rmSync(`${filePath}${suffix}`, { force: true });\\n   221\\t  }\\n   222\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:71:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_33\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba packages/lhc/test/thread-migration.test.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// F-03-001: an existing valid Story 2 thread file (user_version=1, only\\n     2\\t// thread_metadata/event tables) must be migrated to the current schema before\\n     3\\t// any Story 3 message write or read. The fixture reproduces the accepted\\n     4\\t// Story 2 on-disk layout exactly; the assertions go through the production\\n     5\\t// entry points (messageEvents, listMessages, listEvents) plus below-SDK\\n     6\\t// schema-version reads.\\n     7\\t// F-03-002: the lazy opener must reject existing files that are not thread\\n     8\\t// files without creating lhc schema or bumping user_version on them.\\n     9\\timport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n    10\\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n    11\\timport { intakeStream, messages, turns } from \\\"../src/index.js\\\";\\n    12\\timport {\\n    13\\t  legacyEpic01ThreadFile,\\n    14\\t  legacyStory2ThreadFile,\\n    15\\t  openRaw,\\n    16\\t  readDerivedForms,\\n    17\\t  schemaVersionOf,\\n    18\\t  tempStore,\\n    19\\t  validEvent,\\n    20\\t  type TempStore,\\n    21\\t} from \\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\";\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\tlet store: TempStore;\\n    24\\tbeforeEach(() => {\\n    25\\t  store = tempStore();\\n    26\\t});\\n    27\\tafterEach(() => {\\n    28\\t  store.cleanup();\\n    29\\t});\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\tconst legacyEvent = {\\n    32\\t  eventOrder: 1,\\n    33\\t  eventKind: \\\"user_prompt\\\",\\n    34\\t  idempotencyKey: \\\"legacy-key-1\\\",\\n    35\\t  actor: \\\"legacy-actor\\\",\\n    36\\t  harness: \\\"legacy-harness\\\",\\n    37\\t  payload: { text: \\\"recorded before story 3 shipped\\\" },\\n    38\\t  recordedAt: \\\"2026-06-01T00:00:01.000Z\\\",\\n    39\\t};\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tdescribe(\\\"F-03-001: Story 2 thread files migrate before message write/read\\\", () => {\\n    42\\t  it(\\\"messageEvents on a Story 2 file upgrades the schema, keeps the legacy record intact, and projects the new events\\\", async () => {\\n    43\\t    const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n    44\\t    legacyStory2ThreadFile(filePath, \\\"th_legacy01\\\", [legacyEvent]);\\n    45\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(1);\\n    46\\t\\n    47\\t    const result = await intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, [\\n    48\\t      validEvent(\\\"assistant_text\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"answered after upgrade\\\" } }),\\n    49\\t      validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n    50\\t    ]);\\n    51\\t    expect(result.ok).toBe(true);\\n    52\\t    if (!result.ok) return;\\n    53\\t    expect(result.value.events.map((entry) => entry.outcome)).toEqual([\\n    54\\t      \\\"recorded\\\",\\n    55\\t      \\\"recorded\\\",\\n    56\\t    ]);\\n    57\\t    // The order counter continues from the legacy record; the new message id\\n    58\\t    // derives from the continued order.\\n    59\\t    expect(result.value.threadPosition.lastEventOrder).toBe(3);\\n    60\\t    expect(result.value.events[0]!.messageId).toBe(\\\"m2\\\");\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(5);\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t    // The legacy event survives the upgrade byte-for-byte at the SDK level.\\n    65\\t    const events = await intakeStream.listEvents({ filePath });\\n    66\\t    expect(events.ok).toBe(true);\\n    67\\t    if (!events.ok) return;\\n    68\\t    expect(events.value).toHaveLength(3);\\n    69\\t    expect(events.value[0]).toEqual({\\n    70\\t      eventKind: \\\"user_prompt\\\",\\n    71\\t      idempotencyKey: \\\"legacy-key-1\\\",\\n    72\\t      actor: \\\"legacy-actor\\\",\\n    73\\t      harness: \\\"legacy-harness\\\",\\n    74\\t      payload: { text: \\\"recorded before story 3 shipped\\\" },\\n    75\\t      eventOrder: 1,\\n    76\\t      recordedAt: \\\"2026-06-01T00:00:01.000Z\\\",\\n    77\\t    });\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\t    // Projection is intake-time, not retroactive: the new assistant_text\\n    80\\t    // projects; the legacy pre-Story-3 event stays event-only.\\n    81\\t    const projected = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n    82\\t    expect(projected.ok).toBe(true);\\n    83\\t    if (!projected.ok) return;\\n    84\\t    expect(projected.value).toHaveLength(1);\\n    85\\t    expect(projected.value[0]!.messageId).toBe(\\\"m2\\\");\\n    86\\t    expect(projected.value[0]!.sourceEventOrder).toBe(2);\\n    87\\t    expect(projected.value[0]!.blocks).toEqual([\\n    88\\t      { blockType: \\\"text\\\", content: { text: \\\"answered after upgrade\\\" } },\\n    89\\t    ]);\\n    90\\t    expect(projected.value[0]!.tokenEstimate).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    91\\t  });\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t  it(\\\"listMessages on an untouched Story 2 file migrates on read and returns an empty list\\\", async () => {\\n    94\\t    const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n    95\\t    legacyStory2ThreadFile(filePath, \\\"th_legacy02\\\", [legacyEvent]);\\n    96\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(1);\\n    97\\t\\n    98\\t    const projected = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n    99\\t    expect(projected.ok).toBe(true);\\n   100\\t    if (!projected.ok) return;\\n   101\\t    expect(projected.value).toEqual([]);\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(5);\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\t    // The read-path upgrade changed no record content.\\n   106\\t    const events = await intakeStream.listEvents({ filePath });\\n   107\\t    expect(events.ok).toBe(true);\\n   108\\t    if (!events.ok) return;\\n   109\\t    expect(events.value).toHaveLength(1);\\n   110\\t    expect(events.value[0]!.idempotencyKey).toBe(\\\"legacy-key-1\\\");\\n   111\\t  });\\n   112\\t\\n   113\\t  it(\\\"idempotency keys recorded under Story 2 still skip after the upgrade\\\", async () => {\\n   114\\t    const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n   115\\t    legacyStory2ThreadFile(filePath, \\\"th_legacy03\\\", [legacyEvent]);\\n   116\\t\\n   117\\t    const resend = await intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, [\\n   118\\t      validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", {\\n   119\\t        idempotencyKey: \\\"legacy-key-1\\\",\\n   120\\t        payload: { text: \\\"resent after upgrade\\\" },\\n   121\\t      }),\\n   122\\t    ]);\\n   123\\t    expect(resend.ok).toBe(true);\\n   124\\t    if (!resend.ok) return;\\n   125\\t    expect(resend.value.events[0]).toEqual({\\n   126\\t      idempotencyKey: \\\"legacy-key-1\\\",\\n   127\\t      outcome: \\\"skipped\\\",\\n   128\\t      skipReason: \\\"duplicate_idempotency_key\\\",\\n   129\\t    });\\n   130\\t\\n   131\\t    // No message was created for the skipped resend of the legacy event.\\n   132\\t    const projected = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n   133\\t    expect(projected.ok).toBe(true);\\n   134\\t    if (!projected.ok) return;\\n   135\\t    expect(projected.value).toEqual([]);\\n   136\\t  });\\n   137\\t});\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t// Tables present in a file, by name — asserts what schema (if any) the\\n   140\\t// rejected open left behind.\\n   141\\tfunction tableNames(filePath: string): string[] {\\n   142\\t  const db = openRaw(filePath);\\n   143\\t  try {\\n   144\\t    const rows = db\\n   145\\t      .prepare(\\\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = 'table' ORDER BY name\\\")\\n   146\\t      .all() as unknown as Array<{ name: string }>;\\n   147\\t    return rows.map((row) => row.name);\\n   148\\t  } finally {\\n   149\\t    db.close();\\n   150\\t  }\\n   151\\t}\\n   152\\t\\n   153\\tdescribe(\\\"F-03-002: non-thread files are rejected, not adopted\\\", () => {\\n   154\\t  it(\\\"listMessages against an existing empty database file fails without creating schema or bumping user_version\\\", async () => {\\n   155\\t    const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n   156\\t    writeFileSync(filePath, \\\"\\\"); // exists, zero bytes — a valid empty SQLite database\\n   157\\t\\n   158\\t    const result = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n   159\\t    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\\n   160\\t    if (result.ok) return;\\n   161\\t    expect(result.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\"caller_error\\\");\\n   162\\t    expect(result.error.code).toBe(\\\"thread_not_found\\\");\\n   163\\t    expect(result.error.reason).toContain(\\\"not an lhc thread file\\\");\\n   164\\t\\n   165\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(0);\\n   166\\t    expect(tableNames(filePath)).toEqual([]);\\n   167\\t  });\\n   168\\t\\n   169\\t  it(\\\"messageEvents against an unrelated SQLite database fails and leaves its content untouched\\\", async () => {\\n   170\\t    const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n   171\\t    const foreign = openRaw(filePath);\\n   172\\t    try {\\n   173\\t      foreign.exec(\\\"CREATE TABLE notes (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, body TEXT NOT NULL);\\\");\\n   174\\t      foreign.prepare(\\\"INSERT INTO notes (id, body) VALUES (1, ?)\\\").run(\\\"not lhc data\\\");\\n   175\\t    } finally {\\n   176\\t      foreign.close();\\n   177\\t    }\\n   178\\t\\n   179\\t    const result = await intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, [validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\")]);\\n   180\\t    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\\n   181\\t    if (result.ok) return;\\n   182\\t    expect(result.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\"caller_error\\\");\\n   183\\t    expect(result.error.code).toBe(\\\"thread_not_found\\\");\\n   184\\t    expect(result.error.reason).toContain(\\\"not an lhc thread file\\\");\\n   185\\t\\n   186\\t    // No lhc tables were created, the version was not bumped, and the\\n   187\\t    // foreign data is intact.\\n   188\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(0);\\n   189\\t    expect(tableNames(filePath)).toEqual([\\\"notes\\\"]);\\n   190\\t    const db = openRaw(filePath);\\n   191\\t    try {\\n   192\\t      const row = db.prepare(\\\"SELECT body FROM notes WHERE id = 1\\\").get() as unknown as {\\n   193\\t        body: string;\\n   194\\t      };\\n   195\\t      expect(row.body).toBe(\\\"not lhc data\\\");\\n   196\\t    } finally {\\n   197\\t      db.close();\\n   198\\t    }\\n   199\\t  });\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t  it(\\\"a non-SQLite file is rejected as a caller error with its bytes unchanged\\\", async () => {\\n   202\\t    const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n   203\\t    const original = \\\"just some text, definitely not a database\\\\n\\\";\\n   204\\t    writeFileSync(filePath, original);\\n   205\\t\\n   206\\t    const listed = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n   207\\t    expect(listed.ok).toBe(false);\\n   208\\t    if (listed.ok) return;\\n   209\\t    expect(listed.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\"caller_error\\\");\\n   210\\t    expect(listed.error.code).toBe(\\\"thread_not_found\\\");\\n   211\\t\\n   212\\t    const batched = await intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, [validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\")]);\\n   213\\t    expect(batched.ok).toBe(false);\\n   214\\t    if (batched.ok) return;\\n   215\\t    expect(batched.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\"caller_error\\\");\\n   216\\t    expect(batched.error.code).toBe(\\\"thread_not_found\\\");\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\t    expect(readFileSync(filePath, \\\"utf8\\\")).toBe(original);\\n   219\\t  });\\n   220\\t});\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t// Story 0 (Epic 02), FC-0.5 + architecture risk \\\"migration on live data\\\":\\n   223\\t// v5 applies in place to a populated Epic 01 file — existing rows intact,\\n   224\\t// new columns defaulted, the F-02 backfill creating pending derived_form\\n   225\\t// rows for live queued items. A fresh-file migration test would pass while\\n   226\\t// breaking real threads; this one runs over real Epic 01 data.\\n   227\\tdescribe(\\\"FC-0.5: migration v5 over a populated Epic 01 thread file\\\", () => {\\n   228\\t  it(\\\"upgrades in place: records intact, queue columns defaulted, F-02 backfill pending rows present\\\", async () => {\\n   229\\t    const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n   230\\t    legacyEpic01ThreadFile(filePath, \\\"th_epic01\\\");\\n   231\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(4);\\n   232\\t\\n   233\\t    // Any SDK read migrates lazily; the read itself must succeed post-v5.\\n   234\\t    const projected = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n   235\\t    expect(projected.ok).toBe(true);\\n   236\\t    if (!projected.ok) return;\\n   237\\t    expect(schemaVersionOf(filePath)).toBe(5);\\n   238\\t\\n   239\\t    // Existing records intact through the production read surfaces.\\n   240\\t    expect(projected.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\\"m1\\\", \\\"m2\\\", \\\"m3\\\"]);\\n   241\\t    const events = await intakeStream.listEvents({ filePath });\\n   242\\t    expect(events.ok).toBe(true);\\n   243\\t    if (!events.ok) return;\\n   244\\t    expect(events.value).toHaveLength(4);\\n   245\\t    const turnRecords = await turns.listTurns({ filePath });\\n   246\\t    expect(turnRecords.ok).toBe(true);\\n   247\\t    if (!turnRecords.ok) return;\\n   248\\t    expect(turnRecords.value).toEqual([\\n   249\\t      {\\n   250\\t        turnId: \\\"t1\\\",\\n   251\\t        status: \\\"closed\\\",\\n   252\\t        memberMessageIds: [\\\"m1\\\", \\\"m2\\\", \\\"m3\\\"],\\n   253\\t        openedAtEventOrder: 1,\\n   254\\t        closedAtEventOrder: 4,\\n   255\\t      },\\n   256\\t    ]);\\n   257\\t\\n   258\\t    // Work rows survive with their pre-v5 ids; the queue's mechanical\\n   259\\t    // columns exist and default to not-claimed / immediately eligible.\\n   260\\t    const db = openRaw(filePath);\\n   261\\t    try {\\n   262\\t      const items = db\\n   263\\t        .prepare(\\n   264\\t          `SELECT work_item_id, status, attempts, last_error, claimed_at,\\n   265\\t                  claim_expires_at, eligible_at, payload\\n   266\\t           FROM work_item ORDER BY work_item_id`,\\n   267\\t        )\\n   268\\t        .all() as unknown as Array<Record<string, unknown>>;\\n   269\\t      expect(items.map((row) => row.work_item_id)).toEqual([\\n   270\\t        \\\"w-m1-prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n   271\\t        \\\"w-m3-tool_result_summary\\\",\\n   272\\t        \\\"w-t1-turn_derivation\\\",\\n   273\\t      ]);\\n   274\\t      for (const row of items) {\\n   275\\t        expect(row.status).toBe(\\\"queued\\\");\\n   276\\t        expect(Number(row.attempts)).toBe(0);\\n   277\\t        expect(row.last_error).toBeNull();\\n   278\\t        expect(row.claimed_at).toBeNull();\\n   279\\t        expect(row.claim_expires_at).toBeNull();\\n   280\\t        expect(row.eligible_at).toBeNull();\\n   281\\t        expect(row.payload).toBeNull();\\n   282\\t      }\\n   283\\t      // The epic's other v5 surfaces exist (schema ships whole): chunk\\n   284\\t      // tables empty, deleted_at stamps present and null.\\n   285\\t      const chunkCount = db.prepare(\\\"SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM chunk\\\").get() as { n: number | bigint };\\n   286\\t      expect(Number(chunkCount.n)).toBe(0);\\n   287\\t      const deleted = db\\n   288\\t        .prepare(\\\"SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM message WHERE deleted_at IS NOT NULL\\\")\\n   289\\t        .get() as { n: number | bigint };\\n   290\\t      expect(Number(deleted.n)).toBe(0);\\n   291\\t    } finally {\\n   292\\t      db.close();\\n   293\\t    }\\n   294\\t\\n   295\\t    // F-02 backfill: one pending row per live queued item, mapped per kind —\\n   296\\t    // turn_derivation fans out to both turn forms; all at source version 1.\\n   297\\t    expect(\\n   298\\t      readDerivedForms(filePath).map(({ subjectKind, subjectId, form, state, sourceVersion }) => ({\\n   299\\t        subjectKind,\\n   300\\t        subjectId,\\n   301\\t        form,\\n   302\\t        state,\\n   303\\t        sourceVersion,\\n   304\\t      })),\\n   305\\t    ).toEqual([\\n   306\\t      { subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: \\\"m1\\\", form: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\", state: \\\"pending\\\", sourceVersion: 1 },\\n   307\\t      { subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: \\\"m3\\\", form: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\", state: \\\"pending\\\", sourceVersion: 1 },\\n   308\\t      { subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\", subjectId: \\\"t1\\\", form: \\\"lower_band_projection\\\", state: \\\"pending\\\", sourceVersion: 1 },\\n   309\\t      { subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\", subjectId: \\\"t1\\\", form: \\\"turn_rendering\\\", state: \\\"pending\\\", sourceVersion: 1 },\\n   310\\t    ]);\\n   311\\t\\n   312\\t    // The migrated file keeps working through the Epic 01 write path: a new\\n   313\\t    // batch records, projects, and queues against the v5 schema.\\n   314\\t    const batch = await intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, [\\n   315\\t      validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"recorded after the upgrade\\\" } }),\\n   316\\t      validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n   317\\t    ]);\\n   318\\t    expect(batch.ok).toBe(true);\\n   319\\t    if (!batch.ok) return;\\n   320\\t    expect(batch.value.events.map((entry) => entry.outcome)).toEqual([\\\"recorded\\\", \\\"recorded\\\"]);\\n   321\\t    expect(batch.value.queuedWork.map((item) => item.workItemId)).toEqual([\\n   322\\t      \\\"w-m5-prompt_smoothing-v1\\\",\\n   323\\t      \\\"w-t2-turn_derivation-v1\\\",\\n   324\\t    ]);\\n   325\\t  });\\n   326\\t});\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:96:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_46\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- packages/lhc/test/thread-migration.test.ts packages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts packages/lhc/test/cli-process-work-queue.test.ts packages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"diff --git a/packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts b/packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\\nindex fd4d56f..cde83da 100644\\n--- a/packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\\n+++ b/packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\\n@@ -3,16 +3,31 @@ export * as intakeStream from \\\"./domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n export * as messages from \\\"./domains/messages/index.js\\\";\\n export * as turns from \\\"./domains/turns/index.js\\\";\\n \\n+import * as intakeStreamDomain from \\\"./domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n+import * as messagesDomain from \\\"./domains/messages/index.js\\\";\\n+import * as threadsDomain from \\\"./domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\n+import * as turnsDomain from \\\"./domains/turns/index.js\\\";\\n+import { createScheduler, type Scheduler } from \\\"./scheduler.js\\\";\\n+import {\\n+  PROVIDER_OPERATIONS,\\n+  type ResolvedSdkConfig,\\n+  type SdkConfig,\\n+  type WorkHandler,\\n+} from \\\"./shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n+import type { ErrorResult, OpResult } from \\\"./shared/errors.js\\\";\\n+import type { WorkKind } from \\\"./tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\n+\\n export {\\n   estimateTokens,\\n   TOKEN_ESTIMATOR_ID,\\n } from \\\"./tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\n \\n-export type {\\n-  WorkItemRecord,\\n-  WorkKind,\\n-  WorkOwner,\\n-  WorkSourceRef,\\n+export {\\n+  WORK_KIND_REGISTRY,\\n+  type WorkItemRecord,\\n+  type WorkKind,\\n+  type WorkOwner,\\n+  type WorkSourceRef,\\n } from \\\"./tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\n \\n export type {\\n@@ -21,7 +36,29 @@ export type {\\n   ErrorResult,\\n   OpResult,\\n } from \\\"./shared/errors.js\\\";\\n-export type { OperationContext } from \\\"./shared/context.js\\\";\\n+export {\\n+  runInTransaction,\\n+  setSchedulerPoke,\\n+  type OperationContext,\\n+} from \\\"./shared/context.js\\\";\\n+\\n+export type {\\n+  DependencyGap,\\n+  DerivationProvider,\\n+  DerivedForm,\\n+  DerivedFormState,\\n+  FormKind,\\n+  HandlerOutcome,\\n+  HandlerRunContext,\\n+  ProviderResult,\\n+  RenderingPart,\\n+  ResolvedSdkConfig,\\n+  SdkConfig,\\n+  SubjectKind,\\n+  ToolOutcome,\\n+  WorkHandler,\\n+} from \\\"./shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n+export type { Scheduler, SchedulerMode } from \\\"./scheduler.js\\\";\\n \\n export type { ThreadRef } from \\\"./domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\n export type {\\n@@ -36,3 +73,131 @@ export type {\\n   EventRecord,\\n   MessageEventInput,\\n } from \\\"./domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n+\\n+// ── SDK assembly (DD-6/DD-7) ─────────────────────────────────────\\n+\\n+export type WorkHandlerMap = Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>;\\n+\\n+// Merge per-domain handler tables into the one join between the queue's\\n+// opaque kinds and domain code. A kind claimed by two tables is a wiring bug\\n+// (each kind has exactly one owner) and throws at construction.\\n+export function assembleWorkHandlerMap(\\n+  tables: ReadonlyArray<WorkHandlerMap>,\\n+): WorkHandlerMap {\\n+  const map: WorkHandlerMap = {};\\n+  for (const table of tables) {\\n+    for (const [kind, handler] of Object.entries(table)) {\\n+      if (map[kind as WorkKind] !== undefined) {\\n+        throw new TypeError(`work kind \\\"${kind}\\\" registered by more than one domain`);\\n+      }\\n+      map[kind as WorkKind] = handler;\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+  return map;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function unknownWorkKind(kind: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n+  return {\\n+    ok: false,\\n+    error: {\\n+      errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\",\\n+      code: \\\"unknown_work_kind\\\",\\n+      reason: `no handler registered for work kind \\\"${kind}\\\"`,\\n+    },\\n+  };\\n+}\\n+\\n+// Dispatch-time lookup: an unregistered kind is reported explicitly — never\\n+// a throw, never a silent undefined (DD-6, AC-1.8's foundation).\\n+export function lookupWorkHandler(\\n+  map: WorkHandlerMap,\\n+  kind: string,\\n+): OpResult<WorkHandler> {\\n+  const handler = map[kind as WorkKind];\\n+  if (handler === undefined) return unknownWorkKind(kind);\\n+  return { ok: true, value: handler };\\n+}\\n+\\n+export interface Lhc {\\n+  threads: typeof threadsDomain;\\n+  intakeStream: typeof intakeStreamDomain;\\n+  messages: typeof messagesDomain;\\n+  turns: typeof turnsDomain;\\n+  config: ResolvedSdkConfig;\\n+  scheduler: Scheduler;\\n+  workHandlers: WorkHandlerMap;\\n+  lookupWorkHandler(kind: string): OpResult<WorkHandler>;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function requirePositive(value: number, name: string): void {\\n+  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value <= 0) {\\n+    throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: ${name} must be a positive number, got ${value}`);\\n+  }\\n+}\\n+\\n+function requireNonNegative(value: number, name: string): void {\\n+  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value < 0) {\\n+    throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: ${name} must be a non-negative number, got ${value}`);\\n+  }\\n+}\\n+\\n+// The only assembly path: provider, mode, clock, and policy enter here.\\n+// Config mistakes are programmer errors at construction and throw; operating\\n+// failures after construction return OpResults per the error contract.\\n+export function createSdk(config: SdkConfig): Lhc {\\n+  if (config.mode !== \\\"background\\\" && config.mode !== \\\"manual\\\") {\\n+    throw new TypeError(\\n+      `createSdk config: mode must be \\\"background\\\" or \\\"manual\\\", got ${JSON.stringify(config.mode)}`,\\n+    );\\n+  }\\n+  if (config.provider === null || typeof config.provider !== \\\"object\\\") {\\n+    throw new TypeError(\\\"createSdk config: provider must implement DerivationProvider\\\");\\n+  }\\n+  for (const operation of PROVIDER_OPERATIONS) {\\n+    if (typeof config.provider[operation] !== \\\"function\\\") {\\n+      throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: provider is missing operation ${operation}`);\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  const resolved: ResolvedSdkConfig = {\\n+    provider: config.provider,\\n+    mode: config.mode,\\n+    clock: config.clock ?? (() => new Date()),\\n+    retry: config.retry ?? { budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 5000, backoffCapMs: 60000 },\\n+    lease: config.lease ?? { durationMs: 120000 },\\n+    chunkPolicy:\\n+      config.chunkPolicy ?? { targetProjectedTokens: 2200, maxProjectedTokens: 4400 },\\n+  };\\n+  requirePositive(resolved.retry.budget, \\\"retry.budget\\\");\\n+  requireNonNegative(resolved.retry.backoffBaseMs, \\\"retry.backoffBaseMs\\\");\\n+  requireNonNegative(resolved.retry.backoffCapMs, \\\"retry.backoffCapMs\\\");\\n+  if (resolved.retry.backoffCapMs < resolved.retry.backoffBaseMs) {\\n+    throw new TypeError(\\\"createSdk config: retry.backoffCapMs must be >= retry.backoffBaseMs\\\");\\n+  }\\n+  requirePositive(resolved.lease.durationMs, \\\"lease.durationMs\\\");\\n+  requirePositive(resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens, \\\"chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens\\\");\\n+  if (resolved.chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens < resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens) {\\n+    throw new TypeError(\\n+      \\\"createSdk config: chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens must be >= targetProjectedTokens\\\",\\n+    );\\n+  }\\n+\\n+  // Handler maps merge from per-domain contributions at construction (DD-6).\\n+  // The tables are empty until Stories 2–3 land the real handlers; the\\n+  // assembly mechanics are production code from day one.\\n+  const workHandlers = assembleWorkHandlerMap([\\n+    messagesDomain.workHandlers,\\n+    turnsDomain.workHandlers,\\n+  ]);\\n+\\n+  return {\\n+    threads: threadsDomain,\\n+    intakeStream: intakeStreamDomain,\\n+    messages: messagesDomain,\\n+    turns: turnsDomain,\\n+    config: resolved,\\n+    scheduler: createScheduler(resolved.mode),\\n+    workHandlers,\\n+    lookupWorkHandler: (kind) => lookupWorkHandler(workHandlers, kind),\\n+  };\\n+}\\ndiff --git a/packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts b/packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts\\nindex c5b50c0..309c6e0 100644\\n--- a/packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts\\n+++ b/packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts\\n@@ -14,6 +14,69 @@ export function openDatabase(path: string): DatabaseSync {\\n   return db;\\n }\\n \\n+// Epic 02's single migration (tech design §Storage): queue mechanical fields\\n+// on the existing work_item table, the derived_form state table, the chunk\\n+// tables, and the projection-level delete stamps. The whole epic's schema\\n+// lands in one version — behavior arrives story by story. Assembled into the\\n+// thread-file migration history by threads/internal/create.ts.\\n+export const MIGRATION_V5_STATEMENTS: readonly string[] = [\\n+  // claim mechanics on the existing table (DD-1: no disposition column —\\n+  // queue rows are live work only; terminal rows are deleted and their\\n+  // outcomes reported in-memory; durable outcome state lives on derived_form)\\n+  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;`,\\n+  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN last_error TEXT;`,\\n+  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN claimed_at TEXT;`,\\n+  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN claim_expires_at TEXT;`,\\n+  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN eligible_at TEXT;`, // backoff gate; NULL = immediately eligible\\n+  `ALTER TABLE work_item ADD COLUMN payload TEXT;`, // JSON: { sourceVersion?, form? }; id format includes sourceVersion\\n+  // Tech design sketches (status, eligible_at, rowid); SQLite forbids rowid\\n+  // inside an index definition, so the index covers the two real columns and\\n+  // claimNext's ORDER BY rowid walks the head as before.\\n+  `CREATE INDEX idx_work_item_queue ON work_item (status, eligible_at);`,\\n+  `CREATE TABLE derived_form (\\n+    subject_kind TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (subject_kind IN ('message','turn','chunk')),\\n+    subject_id   TEXT NOT NULL,\\n+    form         TEXT NOT NULL,\\n+    state        TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (state IN ('pending','ready','failed','blocked')),\\n+    content      TEXT,\\n+    reason       TEXT,\\n+    metadata     TEXT,\\n+    source_version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\\n+    gaps         TEXT,\\n+    derived_at   TEXT,\\n+    PRIMARY KEY (subject_kind, subject_id, form)\\n+  );`,\\n+  `CREATE TABLE chunk (\\n+    chunk_id     TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n+    chunk_order  INTEGER NOT NULL UNIQUE,\\n+    status       TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('open','closed')),\\n+    accumulated_projected_tokens INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\\n+  );`,\\n+  `CREATE TABLE chunk_member (\\n+    chunk_id   TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES chunk(chunk_id),\\n+    turn_id    TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE REFERENCES turns(turn_id),\\n+    member_idx INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n+    PRIMARY KEY (chunk_id, member_idx)\\n+  );`,\\n+  // projection-level delete (the record keeps everything; reads filter)\\n+  `ALTER TABLE message ADD COLUMN deleted_at TEXT;`,\\n+  `ALTER TABLE turns   ADD COLUMN deleted_at TEXT;`,\\n+  // F-02 backfill: pending form rows for work queued before v5 existed, so\\n+  // UPDATE-only completion finds them (row missing must mean deleted).\\n+  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n+    SELECT 'message', json_extract(source_ref, '$.messageId'), 'smoothed_prompt', 'pending', 1\\n+    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'prompt_smoothing';`,\\n+  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n+    SELECT 'message', json_extract(source_ref, '$.messageId'), 'tool_result_summary', 'pending', 1\\n+    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'tool_result_summary';`,\\n+  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n+    SELECT 'turn', json_extract(source_ref, '$.turnId'), 'turn_rendering', 'pending', 1\\n+    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'turn_derivation';`,\\n+  `INSERT INTO derived_form (subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, source_version)\\n+    SELECT 'turn', json_extract(source_ref, '$.turnId'), 'lower_band_projection', 'pending', 1\\n+    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'turn_derivation';`,\\n+];\\n+\\n export function getSchemaVersion(db: DatabaseSync): number {\\n   const row = db.prepare(\\\"PRAGMA user_version\\\").get() as\\n     | { user_version: number | bigint }\\ndiff --git a/packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts b/packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\\nindex 4449ed7..de96247 100644\\n--- a/packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\\n+++ b/packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\\n@@ -1,22 +1,47 @@\\n-// Durable work-item mechanics: recording and ordered listing, nothing else.\\n-// The util is domain-blind by the tech-arch capability rule — it knows the\\n-// item vocabulary (owner, kind, sourceRef) but nothing about what a turn or\\n-// a summary is; which kinds queue for which sources is the owning domains'\\n-// business. Writes run on the caller's handle inside the batch transaction,\\n-// so items commit (or roll back) with the batch. No public SDK surface:\\n-// read-back reaches here only through the owning domains' listQueuedWork.\\n+// Durable work-item mechanics: recording, ordered listing, and the enqueue\\n+// wrapper that makes \\\"queueing is what schedules processing\\\" structural\\n+// (DD-5). The util is domain-blind by the tech-arch capability rule — it\\n+// knows the item vocabulary (owner, kind, sourceRef) but nothing about what\\n+// a turn or a summary is; which kinds queue for which sources, and which\\n+// derived forms a kind produces, is the owning domains' business (callers\\n+// pass the form targets in). Writes run on the caller's handle inside the\\n+// ambient transaction, so items commit (or roll back) with the batch. No\\n+// public SDK surface: read-back reaches here only through the owning\\n+// domains' listQueuedWork.\\n import type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n+import { fireSchedulerPoke, type OperationContext } from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\n+import type { FormKind, SubjectKind } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n \\n export type WorkOwner = \\\"messages\\\" | \\\"turns\\\";\\n-export type WorkKind = \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\" | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\" | \\\"turn_derivation\\\";\\n-export type WorkSourceRef = { messageId: string } | { turnId: string };\\n+export type WorkKind =\\n+  | \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\"\\n+  | \\\"tool_call_summary\\\"\\n+  | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\"\\n+  | \\\"turn_derivation\\\"\\n+  | \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\"\\n+  | \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\";\\n+export type WorkSourceRef = { messageId: string } | { turnId